    "scientific_justification": "encode_task_id(target_key, semantic_relation) maps strictly to indices [0, 63] indexing one of 6 color-specific named landmarks ('red_box', 'blue_cylinder', 'green_cylinder', 'yellow_cylinder', 'purple_box', 'cyan_cylinder') and 8 relation types ('approach', 'behind', 'in_front', 'left_of', 'right_of', 'multi_waypoint', 'action_probe', 'none'). The network contains no input slot or embedding mechanism to specify which of two visually identical instances (e.g., two identical cyan cylinders) to select. The Phase 5 v4 experiment evaluated 'yellow_cylinder' vs 'cyan_cylinder', which differ in color and category key, and did not correctly install custom obstacle specs in MuJoCo. That historical 5.0% result is therefore INVALIDATED and excluded as valid instance-binding evidence."
